Z||000007||Joe Torma||10-31-2001||12:34 AM||||Dunno...I've been starting/running/driving my car with no dash for 6 months.  Only the Voltmeter needs to be hooked up for the alternator to turn on.<P>Try running a test light to the starter wire on the starter...see if it lights when it is supposed to be cranking.||||reg||1
Z||000008||watts||10-31-2001||01:11 AM||||He's right (uhhh, guy in the first post!).<P>On a 4cyl with DIS, you have to have the speedo hooked up for it to run.  I can't remember why (I spotted it on the schematic somewhere), but the ECM get's pulses fedback through the speedo and it won't run without it.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Monkeyman||10-31-2001||01:20 AM||||Joe Torma--I doubt that you have to have the volt gauge hooked up for the alternator to run.  I haven't had a volt gauge hooked up for a month or better and I don't have any voltage problems (run the headlights alot).  What about cars without volt gauges?  <P>Not trying to flame, just throwing my change in.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Joe Torma||10-31-2001||01:54 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Monkeyman:<BR><B>Joe Torma--I doubt that you have to have the volt gauge hooked up for the alternator to run.  I haven't had a volt gauge hooked up for a month or better and I don't have any voltage problems (run the headlights alot).  What about cars without volt gauges?  <P>Not trying to flame, just throwing my change in.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Flame this Monkeyboy!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif"> <P>Just kidding.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Well, it is actually the idiot light that turns on the alternator...which is part of the voltmeter/rally gauges...that I have plugged in.  What I should have said.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Joe Torma (edited 10-31-2001).]||||reg||8
